<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sohar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Suhar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sohar is a port city on the Batinah coast of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>. In the early Islamic centuries it was one of the great ports of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean-trade">Indian Ocean trade</a>, linking the Gulf with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, and it is often linked with the stories of Sindbad the Sailor. Ahmad ibn Said, founder of the Al Said dynasty, was its governor before becoming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> in the 1740s. It is now a major industrial port.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sohar.jpg" alt="Sohar" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Blue chi (talk) · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sohar-castle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
